------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- ‡µ‡‡Ø‡Ø-‡‡‡ ‚î the round trip is pure cost and trivial meaning.
--
-- The entrypoint note VYAYA_SESA (repo root) argues that complexity is
-- the failure of cost to be a localizing invariant: the groupoid
-- completion L : Derivation ‚í image(ua) sends meaning (eval) down
-- cleanly but cannot carry cost (Laghava).  This module makes the
-- EXACTNESS CRUX of that sequence a checked term, on the kernel's own
-- derivations.
--
-- The kernel of L is generated by the ROUND TRIPS d ‚äï revD d ‚î the
-- loops L collapses to the identity.  The claim of the sequence is that
-- on this kernel, MEANING VANISHES while COST DOES NOT.  Both halves,
-- proved:
--
--   ¬ß1  COST ON THE ROUND TRIP IS 2¬len d ‚î it grows with d, without
--       bound as d grows.  (len-++ then len-revD.)
--   ¬ß2  MEANING ON THE ROUND TRIP IS THE TRIVIAL PATH ‚î for every œ,
--       derivation-sound (d ‚äï revD d) œ ‚â° refl, because it is a loop
--       and meaning lands in a set.
--   ¬ß3  THEREFORE revD IS A DAGGER, NOT AN INVERSE: whenever len d > 0,
--       d ‚äï revD d ‚â done.  Reversal flips direction; it does not
--       cancel.  This is the exact crack ‚î a group inverse would give
--       length 0, and cost forbids it (Laghava, one category down).
--
-- Read as the localization sequence: the round-trip family lands in
-- ker L (meaning trivial, ¬ß2, so L collapses it), yet carries unbounded
-- cost (¬ß1).  A single invariant that is constant where another is
-- unbounded cannot factor through the first: COST DOES NOT DESCEND
-- ALONG L.  That is "cost is the non-localizing residual" as a term,
-- and ¬ß3 names why the completion must add exactly what cost cannot
-- survive.
--
------------------------------------------------------------------------

module VyayaSesa_TheRoundTripIsPureCostAndTrivialMeaningSoCostIsSupportedOnTheKernelOfTheGroupoidCompletion where

